SimpleIPaaS — Agent Handoff Document (Resume Guide)
1) Project Summary
SimpleIPaaS is an enterprise integration platform built on .NET 10 with a layered, clean/domain-driven architecture.

Backend (SimpleIPaaS.Api)
Layers: Domain / Application / Infrastructure / Api
SQLite via EF Core (IPaaSContext) with global multi-tenant query filters (TenantId)
Polly for resilient outbound HTTP calls
Background execution worker runs integration flows
Runtime scripting via Roslyn C# scripting (Microsoft.CodeAnalysis.CSharp.Scripting)
Frontend (SimpleIPaaS.Client)
Blazor WebAssembly
Fluxor state stores: FlowState, ConnectionState, ExecutionState
Node-based flow designer: Z.Blazor.Diagrams
2) Key Architecture Concepts (from prior agent)
Cumulative Named-Node State Pattern
Execution uses a cumulative JSON object (FlowStateContext) throughout the DAG pipeline.
Each node must provide a stable UniqueNodeName / NodeName so outputs are appended under that key.
Dynamic Runtime C# Scripting
Nodes support C# scripts:
Mapping / Transform
Dynamic URL
Pre-flight request body
Post-flight response transform
Branching (boolean result)
Scripts execute via AdvancedCodeExecutionService.cs using Roslyn.
Unified HTTP Action Card
UI moved away from rigid “Source/Destination”
Uses generic HttpActionCard with fields like:
NodeName, UrlCode, PreFlightCode, PostFlightCode
